WEBVTT

00:10.490 --> 00:53.030
The Spring Tournament of Their Youth

00:10.990 --> 00:13.370
Next, we have a special segment.

00:13.370 --> 00:16.830
Chisaka, have you heard of the spring volleyball tournament?

00:16.830 --> 00:18.080
Of course.

00:18.080 --> 00:21.960
It's essentially nationals for volleyball, am I correct?

00:21.960 --> 00:22.840
Yes.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.880
Recently, Miyagi Prefecture held
their qualifiers for the tournament.

00:29.510 --> 00:33.720
This year's matches seems to have had more drama than in previous years.

00:33.720 --> 00:34.970
Indeed.

00:34.970 --> 00:38.100
There are first-years who are making their debut on the national stage,

00:38.100 --> 00:41.020
and third-years who are fighting their final battle in high school.

00:41.020 --> 00:44.570
Each of them must have their own story.

00:45.480 --> 00:51.160
Today, we want to introduce to everyone these high school students who bet their youth on volleyball.

00:56.330 --> 00:58.960
<i>This is a stage for fierce battle.</i>

01:03.210 --> 01:06.920
<i>A place to bet one's youth on—a place to start a challenge.</i>

01:15.850 --> 01:20.100
<i>All three years of high school are encapsulated here.</i>

01:33.490 --> 01:37.990
Japanese National High School Volleyball Tournament

01:34.070 --> 01:36.870
<i>The National High School Volleyball Tournament.</i>

01:37.990 --> 01:39.540
<i>The spring tournament.</i>

01:39.540 --> 01:45.540
<i>The stage where those who dream of making it in volleyball play.</i>

01:53.050 --> 01:56.430
<i>October. It's the beginning of the
qualifiers for the spring tournament.</i>

01:57.640 --> 02:01.890
<i>Koganegawa Kanji is a first-year at Date Tech High School.</i>

02:05.400 --> 02:08.730
<i>He's also one of the challengers aiming to win the spring tournament.</i>

02:15.070 --> 02:17.830
<i>Although he has just started playing volleyball,</i>

02:18.330 --> 02:24.370
<i>he's blessed with being 190 cm tall and having good reflexes.</i>

02:24.370 --> 02:29.590
<i>Serving as the team's on-court playmaker and setter,
he is taking on the spring tournament for the first time.</i>

02:32.470 --> 02:36.430
Mine West              Date Tech

02:32.840 --> 02:36.430
<i>Date Tech's specialty is undoubtedly...</i>

02:36.760 --> 02:37.930
<i>their blocking!</i>

02:42.390 --> 02:44.060
Yeah!

02:44.060 --> 02:49.020
The Iron Wall of Date

02:44.640 --> 02:49.020
<i>The so-called "Iron Wall of Date" terrifies other schools.</i>

02:50.900 --> 02:54.820
<i>In the interhigh qualifiers taking place in summer,</i>

02:54.820 --> 02:59.780
<i>everyone has high expectations for the giant setter Koganegawa because the third-years have retired.</i>

03:00.490 --> 03:08.960
Q: Are you stressed?

03:00.490 --> 03:08.960
Date Tech High School

03:00.490 --> 03:08.960
Setter Koganegawa Kanji (first-year)

03:01.580 --> 03:05.250
Right now, I'm basically a baby as a setter!

03:05.250 --> 03:08.960
But since this important task is
entrusted to me, I will try my best!

03:09.840 --> 03:14.420
<i>As a first-year and a starter,
he will take on nationals for the first time.</i>

03:15.010 --> 03:18.300
<i>We can hear some tension in his words.</i>

03:21.220 --> 03:24.100
<i>The Miyagi Prefecture qualifiers for the spring tournament.</i>

03:25.810 --> 03:30.650
<i>Only one school can advance
through the strait gate to nationals.</i>

03:31.610 --> 03:35.860
<i>Date Tech has demonstrated their tough defense and started off strong.</i>

03:35.860 --> 03:42.120
Shirato                            Date Tech

03:36.610 --> 03:41.330
<i>They have also won the first round of the 16-team tournament.</i>

03:42.540 --> 03:45.290
<i>Then comes the quarterfinals.</i>

03:46.500 --> 03:50.080
<i>Their opponent is the talented Aoba Jousai High School.</i>

03:53.630 --> 03:56.590
<i>Maybe it's because he was nervous for his first spring tournament,</i>

03:56.880 --> 04:00.090
<i>but Koganegawa's movements
became even stiffer than before.</i>

04:02.180 --> 04:07.770
<i>But with the help of his seniors,
he slowly returned to his usual form.</i>

04:11.520 --> 04:13.730
<i>However, in the end,</i>

04:19.240 --> 04:24.080
<i>Koganegawa's block was broken through by his opponent, and the match was over.</i>

04:22.950 --> 04:25.660
Date Tech             Aoba Jousai

04:28.790 --> 04:32.210
It's my fault for messing up!

04:34.000 --> 04:36.670
But next time,

04:37.590 --> 04:42.640
I'll make sure to become the third section
of the Iron Wall so that we can return here!

04:43.350 --> 04:47.430
<i>His first attempt at the spring tournament ended so swiftly.</i>

04:47.430 --> 04:52.310
<i>However, his story is just getting started.</i>

04:54.650 --> 04:56.940
<i>The world of competition is ruthless.</i>

04:56.940 --> 05:00.860
<i>If there is a loser, there must be a winner on the other side.</i>

05:01.910 --> 05:07.750
<i>Date Tech High School was defeated by one of the
favorites for the tournament, Aoba Jousai High School.</i>

05:11.960 --> 05:14.290
<i>As Miyagi Prefecture's best setter,</i>

05:14.290 --> 05:18.630
<i>Oikawa creates a style of volleyball based on combo attacks with his diverse sets.</i>

05:18.630 --> 05:21.130
<i>This is Aoba Jousai's strength.</i>

05:22.760 --> 05:24.760
Team A               Team B

05:28.520 --> 05:30.430
All right, come here for a moment.

05:31.350 --> 05:36.190
<i>During practice, Coach Irihata hardly speaks.</i>

05:37.190 --> 05:44.280
<i>Instead, the third-years, led by their
captain Oikawa, actively drive the team.</i>

05:45.120 --> 05:48.200
The qualifiers are only two weeks away.

05:45.120 --> 05:54.580
Q: Thoughts on the spring tournament?

05:45.120 --> 05:54.580
Aoba Jousai High School

05:45.120 --> 05:54.580
Setter Oikawa Tooru (third-year)

05:48.830 --> 05:50.750
We know exactly what we need to do.

05:51.580 --> 05:54.000
And who we need to defeat.

05:55.170 --> 05:57.630
<i>It's now past 8 pm.</i>

05:57.630 --> 06:01.340
<i>And yet, they keep practicing.</i>

06:02.720 --> 06:07.310
<i>Where does their passion come from?</i>

06:07.310 --> 06:10.890
Unstoppable Force

06:07.850 --> 06:12.230
<i>The persistence needed to take down Shiratorizawa Academy.</i>

06:10.890 --> 06:14.230
Rule the Court

06:17.520 --> 06:21.110
<i>Although Shiratorizawa are the undisputed champions,</i>

06:21.110 --> 06:23.610
Aoba Jousai            Shiratorizawa

06:22.110 --> 06:25.110
<i>Aoba Jousai never stops challenging them.</i>

06:27.070 --> 06:31.000
<i>In the interhigh qualifiers in the summer, the two sides met in the finals.</i>

06:36.250 --> 06:39.960
<i>But that wall was too thick.</i>

06:41.920 --> 06:44.050
<i>Now here in the spring tournament qualifiers,</i>

06:44.050 --> 06:48.050
<i>for the third-years, it's their last chance for revenge.</i>

06:50.640 --> 06:53.560
<i>The semifinals approach.</i>

06:55.810 --> 06:59.690
<i>Their opponent is Miyagi Prefectural Karasuno High School.</i>

06:57.900 --> 07:00.400
Karasuno                    Aoba Jousai

07:01.070 --> 07:06.240
<i>They defeated Karasuno in the third round of the interhigh qualifiers.</i>

07:06.240 --> 07:09.950
<i>As long as they win this match, they can play Shiratorizawa.</i>

07:18.960 --> 07:25.970
<i>However, in the first set, under the onslaught of Karasuno, they could only defend passively and lost.</i>

07:28.720 --> 07:30.850
Karasuno                    Aoba Jousai

07:38.440 --> 07:42.480
<i>Despite this, due to their extensive experience, Aoba Jousai did not become anxious.</i>

07:43.400 --> 07:48.990
<i>They never doubted what they believe in and kept playing their own style.</i>

07:58.710 --> 08:00.500
<i>The match seesawed back and forth.</i>

08:00.500 --> 08:03.670
<i>Then, they reached the third and final set.</i>

08:03.670 --> 08:08.260
<i>After an endless deuce, the levy finally broke.</i>

08:13.640 --> 08:15.430
<i>The dream of taking on nationals ended.</i>

08:15.430 --> 08:20.020
<i>Oikawa's best attempt at setting up a play was shut down.</i>

08:20.020 --> 08:20.980
<i>They lost.</i>

08:26.030 --> 08:28.530
<i>They were unable to challenge Shiratorizawa,</i>

08:28.530 --> 08:32.160
<i>and Oikawa's challenge for the spring tournament ended here.</i>

08:32.740 --> 08:36.870
<i>Yet he kept his head held high and looked straight forward.</i>

08:38.620 --> 08:39.750
It's unfortunate that we lost,

08:40.620 --> 08:45.710
but I have faith our juniors will avenge us next year.

08:49.550 --> 08:52.510
The Japanese National High School Boys' Volleyball Tournament Miyagi Prefecture Qualifier

08:49.550 --> 08:52.510
Finals

08:49.550 --> 08:52.510
Shiratorizawa
vs.
Karasuno

08:50.760 --> 08:54.510
<i>Then comes the match that opens up the path to nationals: the finals.</i>

08:55.600 --> 08:58.600
<i>Facing Karasuno, who keep on winning,</i>

08:58.600 --> 09:01.400
<i>are the undisputed champions, Shiratorizawa,</i>

09:01.400 --> 09:06.320
<i>known all across the country after racking up
countless victories via their overwhelming strength.</i>

09:33.470 --> 09:37.520
<i>No one doubted that Shiratorizawa would be victorious.</i>

09:37.520 --> 09:41.850
<i>But within the match, there was a twist in the story.</i>

09:43.060 --> 09:48.440
<i>After the fierce battle in the final set, the champions, Shiratorizawa, were defeated by Karasuno.</i>

09:50.490 --> 09:52.400
<i>First it was Aoba Jousai.</i>

09:52.400 --> 09:56.870
<i>Now Karasuno High School has upset Shiratorizawa,</i>

09:57.240 --> 10:00.540
<i>punching their ticket to nationals.</i>

10:03.080 --> 10:07.710
<i>They were once called "the fallen champs" and "the clipped crows."</i>

10:07.710 --> 10:09.880
<i>What is the secret that let them take flight?</i>

10:11.720 --> 10:15.050
<i>Karasuno High School,
who qualified for the spring tournament,</i>

10:16.390 --> 10:18.890
<i>is an extremely ordinary public high school.</i>

10:26.110 --> 10:30.070
<i>They were once called "the fallen champs" and "the clipped crows."</i>

10:30.070 --> 10:33.700
<i>Where can the secret to their newfound flight be found?</i>

10:33.700 --> 10:35.200
Nice spike!

10:36.570 --> 10:37.780
Nice spike!

10:38.780 --> 10:40.790
<i>There are currently 12 members on the team.</i>

10:39.370 --> 10:40.370
Here it comes!

10:41.410 --> 10:43.290
<i>Although it can't be called a big team,</i>

10:44.040 --> 10:48.790
<i>after watching their practice, the first thing that can be noticed is their excellent teamwork.</i>

10:52.260 --> 10:59.260
<i>No matter how difficult the moment, Captain Sawamura shouts louder and clearer than everyone else.</i>

10:52.630 --> 10:54.130
Use your voices!

10:55.470 --> 10:56.680
Yessir!

10:56.680 --> 10:57.550
Let's continue!

10:59.970 --> 11:06.060
<i>And then there is Sugawara,
who assists the sometimes harsh Sawamura.</i>

11:02.060 --> 11:03.640
Nice spike!

11:03.640 --> 11:05.310
Don't lose to Daichi!

11:05.310 --> 11:06.600
Right!

11:07.560 --> 11:10.440
<i>Then there's the life of the party, Tanaka.</i>

11:12.530 --> 11:16.820
<i>And Nishinoya, who uses his energetic
performances to motivate his teammates.</i>

11:13.490 --> 11:15.700
Ryuu, are you afraid of the cameras?

11:15.700 --> 11:16.820
That was weak!

11:16.820 --> 11:18.320
I'm not afraid!

11:18.320 --> 11:37.260
Q: Why has Karasuno taken flight?

11:18.320 --> 11:37.260
Karasuno High School Coach Ukai Keishin

11:20.870 --> 11:24.500
Well, the first-years all have spunk.

11:24.500 --> 11:29.250
Oh, three of the four first-years are starters.

11:29.250 --> 11:36.680
Maybe the team can make the most of their abilities because the upperclassmen paved the way for them.

11:38.220 --> 11:41.720
<i>Surprisingly, they have three first-years as starters.</i>

11:42.510 --> 11:48.270
<i>It seems the key to the crows taking flight lies within these four spunky first-years.</i>

11:49.360 --> 11:54.650
<i>One of them is Kageyama Tobio,
starting setter despite being a first-year.</i>

11:59.200 --> 12:05.330
<i>His amazing setting skills have been well-known since his time at the famous Kitagawa First Junior High.</i>

12:08.670 --> 12:13.300
<i>And in the match against Shiratorizawa, his sets were just as clean.</i>

12:13.300 --> 12:23.010
Q: Any reflections on the Shiratorizawa match?

12:13.300 --> 12:23.010
Karasuno High School

12:13.300 --> 12:23.010
Setter Kageyama Tobio (first-year)

12:14.800 --> 12:17.680
Uh, well, they were really good.

12:18.380 --> 12:20.890
Um, can I get back to practice?

12:23.890 --> 12:29.940
<i>The second first-year is Tsukishima Kei,
the tallest member of the team and a middle blocker.</i>

12:30.480 --> 12:35.070
<i>He's usually rather reserved and doesn't like having to deal with other people.</i>

12:36.150 --> 12:41.620
Q: Are you always that reserved?

12:36.150 --> 12:41.620
Karasuno High School

12:36.150 --> 12:41.620
Middle Blocker Tsukishima Kei (first-year)

12:37.150 --> 12:40.280
Yeah. I mean, uh... yeah.

12:43.410 --> 12:45.620
<i>However, his performance in the match was full of passion,</i>

12:46.120 --> 12:50.290
<i>in complete contrast to the attitude he shows on the surface.</i>

12:51.540 --> 12:54.840
<i>He kept jumping up to block, over and over.</i>

12:56.130 --> 12:58.470
<i>Until his fingers became scarred.</i>

12:59.170 --> 13:00.010
<i>And then...</i>

13:02.430 --> 13:07.980
<i>It was a block bet on the will of his teammates, as well as his own pride.</i>

13:08.350 --> 13:11.650
All right!

13:12.350 --> 13:14.980
<i>The third first-year is Yamaguchi Tadashi.</i>

13:15.940 --> 13:18.690
<i>His position is pinch server.</i>

13:18.690 --> 13:24.200
<i>He plays a critical role in turning the tables
during a set where the opponent has momentum.</i>

13:26.290 --> 13:39.260
Q: Do you feel nervous?

13:26.290 --> 13:39.260
Karasuno High School

13:26.290 --> 13:39.260
Middle Blocker Yamaguchi Tadashi (first-year)

13:28.200 --> 13:30.620
Uh, yeah, I do.

13:30.620 --> 13:38.170
But when I stand in position to serve, I tell myself that it's now or never.

13:44.180 --> 13:46.560
<i>A body that can't move freely,</i>

13:47.180 --> 13:49.390
<i>afraid what will happen if he fails.</i>

13:51.390 --> 13:54.610
<i>Even so, Yamaguchi overcame the fear...</i>

13:55.440 --> 13:56.770
<i>by believing in himself!</i>

13:59.400 --> 14:02.110
Yes!

14:09.160 --> 14:13.170
<i>The last first-year is Hinata Shouyou, a middle blocker.</i>

14:14.580 --> 14:21.800
<i>Although he's only 163 cm tall,
he's shown he can put in the work to play that position.</i>

14:23.130 --> 14:27.810
<i>He says he started playing volleyball because he admired the Little Giant.</i>

14:30.100 --> 14:34.900
<i>Even so, outside of volleyball,
he's just your average high school student.</i>

14:38.440 --> 14:39.900
Okay, Hinata. Your turn.

14:39.900 --> 14:42.820
Fill in the parentheses with a vegetable you hate and read it out loud.

14:42.820 --> 14:44.360
R-Right!

14:44.740 --> 14:50.870
The vegetable that I don't like is piiman!

14:50.870 --> 14:53.910
That's called a "green pepper" in English.

14:53.910 --> 14:56.830
What you said sounds like "pee man."

15:02.840 --> 15:06.340
<i>But once he appears on the court,</i>

15:06.340 --> 15:08.600
Give it to me!

15:06.760 --> 15:07.640
<i>he takes flight!</i>

15:09.010 --> 15:09.930
<i>He flies!</i>

15:11.390 --> 15:12.060
<i>Fly!</i>

15:20.270 --> 15:27.570
<i>And what crushes the idea; of the undisputed champions of Shiratorizawa is his right hand.</i>

15:29.320 --> 15:31.620
Shiratorizawa

15:29.320 --> 15:31.620
Karasuno

15:31.620 --> 15:43.090
Q: Any thoughts on the final point?

15:31.910 --> 15:34.910
Ushiwaka's cross-court spike was sick!

15:34.910 --> 15:43.090
When planning that final attack, I waited patiently at first, and then rushed forward with everyone with a "bam"!

15:44.460 --> 15:50.050
<i>Where they cultivate teamwork isn't limited to the court or the clubroom.</i>

15:51.100 --> 15:57.100
Foot of the Slope

15:52.810 --> 15:55.060
Hurry home after eating.

15:55.060 --> 15:56.350
Yes, sir!

15:57.100 --> 16:02.820
Q: What about dinner?

15:59.310 --> 16:01.190
Of course, I'll eat dinner when I get back!

16:01.190 --> 16:02.820
This is just a snack!

16:02.820 --> 16:06.030
<i>Let's take a look at how Hinata scarfs down his food.</i>

16:02.820 --> 16:13.290
Q: Is it delicious?

16:06.030 --> 16:08.820
<i>He truly is a Little Giant.</i>

16:08.820 --> 16:12.870
Wow! The meat buns that the
captain treats us to are awesome!

16:12.870 --> 16:16.120
Hey, I didn't say anything about paying for them!

16:16.120 --> 16:18.790
In that case, today it'll be my treat.

16:20.250 --> 16:22.210
Daichi, can you cover me too?

16:23.340 --> 16:26.920
Didn't I say to eat after paying?!

16:26.920 --> 16:31.220
Coach, please treat us this time to celebrate our victory!

16:28.010 --> 16:33.850
<i>The key to Karasuno High School's flight seems to be the relationship between the seniors and juniors—</i>

16:33.850 --> 16:38.100
<i>an environment where you can play together happily.</i>

16:41.020 --> 16:47.110
<i>In this way, Karasuno High School set off a whirlwind
in the tournament and printed their ticket to nationals.</i>

16:48.070 --> 16:51.910
<i>In their hearts, there is a dream that needs to come true.</i>

16:53.700 --> 16:56.330
<i>Nekoma Metropolitan High School.</i>

16:57.120 --> 17:02.330
<i>A powerhouse school in the tough division of Tokyo, they've advanced to national numerous times.</i>

17:02.880 --> 17:05.380
<i>They're led by Coach Nekomata,</i>

17:05.380 --> 17:11.390
<i>who was rivals with the former Karasuno
coach that led them to nationals, Ukai Ikkei.</i>

17:12.840 --> 17:18.350
<i>The two teams have always been rivals and held a training camp together during summer vacation.</i>

17:19.140 --> 17:22.060
<i>But despite having such a long relationship,</i>

17:22.560 --> 17:26.320
<i>the two schools have never played
against each other in an official match.</i>

17:28.740 --> 17:33.120
<i>May they one day face off against each other at nationals.</i>

17:34.120 --> 17:44.580
Q: Can you say a few words to Karasuno?

17:34.120 --> 17:44.580
Nekoma Metropolitan High School

17:34.120 --> 17:44.580
Captain Kuroo Tetsurou (third-year)

17:34.780 --> 17:37.830
Congrats on advancing to the spring tournament.

17:37.830 --> 17:44.040
We'll definitely win the Tokyo qualifiers and make the Battle of the Garbage Dumpster a reality.

17:45.380 --> 17:52.010
<i>Will the goddess of battle let these
two fated schools meet on the court?</i>

17:53.550 --> 17:58.060
<i>The Tokyo qualifiers start in November.</i>

18:06.270 --> 18:09.320
We're gonna win the spring tournament!

18:09.320 --> 18:11.150
Yeah!

18:12.780 --> 18:17.580
<i>Ever eager to improve, the players have a passionate soul.</i>

18:17.580 --> 18:20.910
<i>That's the reward for their diligent efforts.</i>

18:28.340 --> 18:30.630
<i>The spring tournament's orange court—</i>

18:31.550 --> 18:36.640
<i>the stage where dreams of youth are made or broken.</i>

18:41.140 --> 18:44.520
<i>The rivals who fight hard on the court</i>

18:45.770 --> 18:50.110
<i>are also buddies who share the same dream.</i>

19:41.950 --> 19:47.420
<i>With that dream on its wings, the crow now takes flight!</i>

19:52.920 --> 19:57.090
Man, your youth really is a special time.

19:57.090 --> 20:00.510
It reminds me of my high school days.

20:00.510 --> 20:02.720
Yes, me too.

20:02.720 --> 20:07.980
I hope that Karasuno High School can work hard on behalf of their defeated opponents.

20:08.980 --> 20:11.520
We hope you were satisfied with today's special.

20:11.520 --> 20:15.440
We look forward to your feedback.

20:15.110 --> 20:16.400
It's over?!

20:15.440 --> 20:20.200
We will draw a name from among those who provide feedback to win a special sticker made for—

20:20.990 --> 20:23.540
I was barely in it at all.

20:23.540 --> 20:26.500
I was just mentioned in passing when they were introducing our team.

20:26.500 --> 20:29.580
My name wasn't even mentioned.

20:30.290 --> 20:31.460
Don't let it get to you, Asahi.

20:31.460 --> 20:32.630
He's right.

20:32.630 --> 20:35.420
Your job is to spike the ball.

20:36.050 --> 20:39.680
Kageyama, you looked so unfriendly. It creeped me out!

20:39.680 --> 20:41.970
Huh?! What'd you say, moron?!

20:41.970 --> 20:43.930
C'mon. Let's get back to practice.

20:43.930 --> 20:45.180
Right!

20:49.350 --> 20:51.860
Goodbye!

20:56.440 --> 22:28.330
Special! The Spring Tournament of Their Youth

20:56.440 --> 22:28.330
Karasuno High School vs. Shiratorizawa Academy

20:56.440 --> 22:28.330
Haikyuu
